sys/include/ape/c++ -- EDC C++ language support and the first APExp C++ library.

The EDG language-support headers (*.stdh) are copied from
sys/src/external/edg/include_c++. They provide compiler-specific support
such as new/delete declarations, RTTI, exceptions, and initializer_list.
The ABI runtime is libedg.a in sys/src/ape/lib/edg.

Paragon Portable STL has been merged into this directory. Its component
headers retain their upstream subdirectory organization, while public
EDC include names such as <vector> resolve through vector.stdh. The
implementation namespace is std. This is an initial port, not a claim of
complete C++ standard-library conformance; see docs/notes/cxx-library.md
for known API differences, integration work, and the staged roadmap.

The EDG copies can be checked against upstream with:

    diff -rq -x README sys/include/ape/c++ sys/src/external/edg/include_c++

Differences reported under the merged STL are expected. Restrict the
comparison to the language-support headers when checking EDG provenance.
